d}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186115744 "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+\\sqrt{7}y=0.3 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y=\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The lines $3x+\\sqrt{7}y=0.3$ and $-2\\sqrt{0.1}x+3y=\\sqrt{7}$ intersect exactly at one point\n\n- **II.** The determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $0$\n\n- **III.** The coefficient matrix is invertible"] [#edb/ref 17592186115753 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+4y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186115830 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=-2 \\\\ x+y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186115831 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+3)y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186115832 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [#edb/ref 17592186115882 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 2, & x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It is **not** continuous at $x=1$ but it is differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **III.** It is **not** differentiable on the interval $x\\in (-2,2)$"] 