m of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=8 \\\\ x-2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186192588 "Find the solution $(u,v)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5u-6v=3 \\\\ -3u+2v=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186193073 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[5X-2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & 1\\le x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186193226 "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=0 \\\\ 2x-3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: Eliminate the variable $x.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186193242 "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ s+5t=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations."] [#edb/ref 17592186193285 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y=11 \\\\ 7x+4y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $y.$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186198228 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{x^2}{24} + \\dfrac{y^2}{24} +\\dfrac{z^2}{6} = 1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=8t, \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}$ \nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186198998 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=1-t, \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186221169 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\