rix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [#edb/ref 17592186229682 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186229684 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186234005 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+b\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+cx+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=2.$ What is the value of the constants $b$ and $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186234014 "Let $f