er the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v=-3 \\\\ u=-v-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496233 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3u+z=-2 \\\\ 3u-5z=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $u$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-3u+5z=17.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=15.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(u,z)$ of the system."] [#edb/ref 17592186496235 "Find the solution $(p,q)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-4p-5q=1 \\\\ 4p+2q=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496237 "Using the elimination method, eliminate the variable $b$ and find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5a-b=19 \\\\ 3a+b=21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496243 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What are the modes of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{3\\pi +2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3\\pi  \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496247 "![](images/5c/5c6e4deccce395f5bdc8aadef8cd2c712804235c340ccae174f2067211a5a49c.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ {x}^{2}+y, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496248 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n