 \\\\ 10, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor what value of $b$ is the function continuous at $x=0?$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504608 "Find the $72.9$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504611 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{cx+4}, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{27}, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504614 "The function $f(x)$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{x+3}, & x\\ne -3 \\\\ 2, & x=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nhas an  infinite discontinuity at $x=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504616 "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504617 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6k-20{x}^{2}, & x\\ne 1, \\\\ -8, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$ \n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504620 "The function $h(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x-c)^{2}+1, & x\\ne 2, \\\\ 2, & x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$, what are the possible values of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504621 "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+k}-\\sqrt{k}}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 18, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504628 "The function $f(x)$ is defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+k}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 2, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504630 "The function $g(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2x+a}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 36, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504631 "Find all of the points where $f(x)$ below has an infinite discontinuity.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-x, & x\\le 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x-3}, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504635 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4y=2x.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and ${y}_{2}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we should seek a particular solution \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the following constraints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2}^{′}=2x \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{y}_{1}+{u}_{2}^{′}{y}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that ${u}_{1}(x)=-\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ find the function $g.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504638 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3a-2ax, & x\\ne -2, \\\\ 14, & x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2,$ what is the value of $a?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504646 "Find the $60$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504647 "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡3(x-k), & x\\ne 1, \\\\ 2, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504651 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{x-2}, & x\\ne 4, \\\\ c, & x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4,$ what is the value of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504667 "The function $f(x)$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1, & x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{x-1}, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nhas an  infinite discontinuity at $x=${{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504674 "From **left to right**, the $x$-values  where the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5-x}, & x<5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-x}, & x\\ge 5,\\,x\\ne 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n has an infinite discontinuity are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,$ $x=$\n{{field-2}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186504676 "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504677 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(a-x)^{2}-a, & x\\ne -3, \\\\ 9, & x=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3,$ **in ascending order**, what are the possible values of $a?$\n\n$a=$ \n{{field-1}}\nor\n$a=$ \n{{field-2}}"] [#edb/ref 17592186504699 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(c-x)^{2}+3c, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ -5, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$, what are the possible values of $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504702 "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186504708 "Find all of the points where $f(x)$ below has infinite discontinuities.\n\n$$\nf(x)=