}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519545 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2y}{12}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519548 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519563 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3x, & \\,y<x<1\\,,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{6}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519568 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{5}<X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{4}{3}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519578 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5y\\sqrt{x}, & 0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x\\sqrt{x}}{2}, & 0<x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0<x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519584 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}y\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(\\frac{1}{4}<Y<X\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519592 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{10}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9}{10}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{X}(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519605 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{14}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186519607 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3y}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y+1}{8}, & 0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for which the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ and the marginal density function ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520449 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+2{y}^{2})}{5}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1.5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1.5)$ is shown above."] [#edb/ref 17592186520451 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+{y}^{2})}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+1}{8}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520452 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(x+y)}{5}, & x\\le y\\le 2x,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520453 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{5}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520458 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+2y}{3}, & \\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above."] [#edb/ref 17592186520462 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0<x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}24{x}^{2}, & 0<x<\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520463 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}-y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520464 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y+2}{5}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0<y<1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520466 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+4y}{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520474 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520489 "$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}, & \\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above."] [#edb/ref 17592186520491 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{12}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. 